WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.234 --> 00:00:02.400
-Welcome, everybody.
Welcome, welcome,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:03.567
welcome to "The Tonight Show."

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.334
You're here,
and I appreciate it.

00:00:05.334 --> 00:00:07.634
Thank you for watching.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:10.167
Guys, today is Friday the 13th.

00:00:10.167 --> 00:00:12.100
[ Audience "Oohs" ]

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:14.634
This morning -- This morning,
I thought a black cat

00:00:14.634 --> 00:00:17.234
jumped in front of me,
but thank God it was just a rat.

00:00:17.234 --> 00:00:20.868
[ Laughter ]
I go -- oof!

00:00:20.868 --> 00:00:23.634
All right, now let's get to
20 jokes about Taylor Swift.

00:00:23.634 --> 00:00:24.901
All right.
Last night --

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:26.334
[ Scattered cheers, laughter ]

00:00:26.334 --> 00:00:28.267
That's all we've been
talking about it all week.

00:00:28.267 --> 00:00:30.133
Last night, for the third time
this season,

00:00:30.133 --> 00:00:32.801
Taylor Swift
was cheering on Travis Kelce

00:00:32.801 --> 00:00:34.801
at the Kansas City Chiefs game.

00:00:34.801 --> 00:00:36.334
[ Cheers ]
Yep, yep.

00:00:36.334 --> 00:00:39.767
The NFL has the biggest pop star
in the world at its games,

00:00:39.767 --> 00:00:41.000
while Major League Baseball's
like,

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:43.000
"We have...live organ music."

00:00:43.000 --> 00:00:45.067
[ Laughter ]

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:49.234
♪ Dan dan dan dan,
dan dan dan dan ♪

00:00:49.234 --> 00:00:52.400
♪ Dan dan dan dan,
dan dan ♪

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.534
Then it goes...
♪ Da da da... ♪

00:00:55.534 --> 00:00:57.267
Doesn't it?
[ Musical flourish ]

00:00:57.267 --> 00:00:58.868
No, all right.
Not everyone can do it.

00:00:58.868 --> 00:01:00.267
Not everyone can do it.
It's a hard --

00:01:00.267 --> 00:01:02.434
-Almost.
-Not everyone can do it.

00:01:02.434 --> 00:01:03.834
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.834 --> 00:01:05.300
-Well, he doesn't do it
for a living.

00:01:05.300 --> 00:01:07.300
-That's all right.
That's all right.

00:01:07.300 --> 00:01:09.767
It's very hard.
Very hard.

00:01:09.767 --> 00:01:11.667
Say what you want
about this relationship,

00:01:11.667 --> 00:01:14.667
but flying to Kansas City on
a Thursday night, that's love.

00:01:14.667 --> 00:01:16.067
-Yeah.
-Yeah. That's love.

00:01:16.067 --> 00:01:19.100
Taylor watched the game
with Travis's mom and dad.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:20.968
That's a fun date, huh?
"You want to spend four hours

00:01:20.968 --> 00:01:22.467
with my parents
while I play with my friends?"

00:01:22.467 --> 00:01:26.167
"All right.
Not really, not really."

00:01:26.167 --> 00:01:28.634
Meanwhile, before the game,
announcer Al Michaels promised

00:01:28.634 --> 00:01:30.067
that they wouldn't go overboard

00:01:30.067 --> 00:01:31.734
with their coverage
of Taylor Swift.

00:01:31.734 --> 00:01:33.033
Let's see how they did.

00:01:33.033 --> 00:01:36.100
-In case you are wondering,
Taylor Swift is here.

00:01:36.100 --> 00:01:38.601
-Of course, his number-one fan,
Taylor Swift,

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:40.467
is here in Arrowhead
to cheer him on.

00:01:40.467 --> 00:01:44.734
-Looking on is his good buddy
and girlfriend, Taylor Swift.

00:01:44.734 --> 00:01:45.968
Word just came down to me

00:01:45.968 --> 00:01:47.667
that Taylor Swift has written
a couple of songs

00:01:47.667 --> 00:01:48.801
for us tonight.

00:01:48.801 --> 00:01:50.000
Well, everything in moderation,

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:51.701
but here's another shot
of Taylor Swift.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:52.901
[ Laughter ]
-Yeah.

00:01:52.901 --> 00:01:55.033
-Yeah, honestly,
compared to the last two games,

00:01:55.033 --> 00:01:56.968
mission accomplished.
I mean, well done.

00:01:56.968 --> 00:01:58.868
They barely -- they cut --

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:01.968
The final score was Chiefs 19,
Broncos 8,

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:04.033
cutaways to Taylor 572.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.934
[ Laughter ]

00:02:05.934 --> 00:02:08.200
Well, guys, the three big movies
this weekend are

00:02:08.200 --> 00:02:10.234
"Taylor Swift: The Eras Tour,"
the --

00:02:10.234 --> 00:02:11.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:11.901 --> 00:02:12.934
It's gonna be giant.

00:02:12.934 --> 00:02:15.234
"The Exorcist."
-Ooh!

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:17.267
-And "Saw."
-Oh.

00:02:17.267 --> 00:02:18.934
-Yeah, and since
it's Friday the 13th,

00:02:18.934 --> 00:02:20.634
we thought we'd combine
them all together,

00:02:20.634 --> 00:02:23.133
so please enjoy.

00:02:23.133 --> 00:02:25.334
♪♪

00:02:25.334 --> 00:02:28.133
-♪'Cause baby's got bad blood ♪

00:02:28.133 --> 00:02:30.834
♪ You know it used to be
bad love ♪

00:02:30.834 --> 00:02:33.801
♪ So take a look at
what you've done ♪

00:02:33.801 --> 00:02:36.400
♪ 'Cause, baby, now we got
bad blood ♪

00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.267
Hey.

00:02:37.267 --> 00:02:38.567
-[ Roars ]
-Unh!

00:02:38.567 --> 00:02:39.734
[ Audience groans ]

00:02:39.734 --> 00:02:41.267
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:41.267 --> 00:02:43.634
-Happy Friday --
[ Laughs ]

00:02:43.634 --> 00:02:46.667
Happy Friday the 13th.

00:02:46.667 --> 00:02:48.033
Well, some political news.

00:02:48.033 --> 00:02:51.133
After failing to gain
enough support from Republicans,

00:02:51.133 --> 00:02:52.467
Congressman Steve Scalise

00:02:52.467 --> 00:02:55.801
has dropped out of the race
for House speaker.

00:02:55.801 --> 00:02:58.601
Yeah, if we're using Republicans
to measure time,

00:02:58.601 --> 00:03:01.100
a Scalise is even shorter
than a Scaramucci.

00:03:01.100 --> 00:03:03.567
[ Laughter ]

00:03:03.567 --> 00:03:05.467
"I just came in
for a quick Scalise.

00:03:05.467 --> 00:03:08.300
It wasn't a full Scaramucci.
It was..."

00:03:08.300 --> 00:03:09.667
[ Laughter ]

00:03:09.667 --> 00:03:11.767
The House is a mess,
McCarthy got voted out,

00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:13.501
Scalise couldn't
get enough votes,

00:03:13.501 --> 00:03:15.567
and the interim speaker
slams the gavel

00:03:15.567 --> 00:03:17.334
like he's playing
Whac-A-Mole.

00:03:18.634 --> 00:03:22.000
[ Laughter ]

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:23.667
That's right. The search
for a new speaker

00:03:23.667 --> 00:03:26.334
has been pretty chaotic.
First, it was Kevin McCarthy,

00:03:26.334 --> 00:03:28.367
then it was Steve Scalise,
and now it doesn't seem

00:03:28.367 --> 00:03:30.200
like anyone else
can get enough votes.

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:33.133
But tonight, the House
finally picked a new nominee,

00:03:33.133 --> 00:03:35.734
and he's here now,
via satellite, from D.C.

00:03:35.734 --> 00:03:38.400
Please welcome the new pick
for speaker of the House,

00:03:38.400 --> 00:03:40.734
Tim Barrett.
Tim, thank you for being here.

00:03:40.734 --> 00:03:43.100
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:45.000
-Thanks for having me, Jimmy.

00:03:45.000 --> 00:03:46.567
I'm very excited
to represent my party

00:03:46.567 --> 00:03:48.133
and my country
in this new role,

00:03:48.133 --> 00:03:50.367
and I'm ready to hit
the ground running.

00:03:50.367 --> 00:03:53.234
-Now, Tim, what would you say
your biggest goals

00:03:53.234 --> 00:03:56.200
are as you take over
the office of speaker?

00:03:56.200 --> 00:03:58.100
-Great question. Jimmy.

00:03:58.100 --> 00:04:00.634
I think that, above all,
we need to come together --

00:04:00.634 --> 00:04:02.267
-Yeah, yeah, I'm sorry.
Hang on. I'm sorry.

00:04:02.267 --> 00:04:04.234
What's going on?
What happened to Tim?

00:04:04.234 --> 00:04:06.934
-Oh, he dropped out.
-Just --

00:04:06.934 --> 00:04:08.434
Just now he dropped out?

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.000
-That's right.
I'm the new nominee,

00:04:10.000 --> 00:04:12.133
and I couldn't be more excited
to get started.

00:04:12.133 --> 00:04:14.367
-Yeah, yeah, okay.
But I'm sorry, but who are you?

00:04:14.367 --> 00:04:16.467
-My name is Bill Doyle.

00:04:16.467 --> 00:04:19.434
-Okay, Bill,
I'm a little thrown off,

00:04:19.434 --> 00:04:21.334
but I guess I'll ask you
the same thing.

00:04:21.334 --> 00:04:23.934
What are your biggest goals
as speaker?

00:04:23.934 --> 00:04:26.100
-Party unity, Jimmy.

00:04:26.100 --> 00:04:27.567
That's where it all starts.

00:04:27.567 --> 00:04:29.434
-Yeah. I'm sorry. Wait.
Who are you?

00:04:29.434 --> 00:04:30.734
-I'm Jordan Roth,

00:04:30.734 --> 00:04:33.234
the new nominee
for speaker of the House.

00:04:33.234 --> 00:04:35.734
-You're the new
speaker nominee?

00:04:35.734 --> 00:04:37.267
-That's right, Jimmy.

00:04:37.267 --> 00:04:39.434
Hank Remington.
Nice to meet you.

00:04:39.434 --> 00:04:41.801
-I'm sorry. Wait.
Another nominee for speaker?

00:04:41.801 --> 00:04:43.434
That's, like the fourth one
in a minute.

00:04:43.434 --> 00:04:44.868
How is this even happening?

00:04:44.868 --> 00:04:48.167
-I know. It's a little cuckoo
around here, L-O-L.

00:04:48.167 --> 00:04:49.868
-Wait. I'm sorry.
Tim?

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:52.434
You're here again?
You're back in the running?

00:04:52.434 --> 00:04:54.434
-No, I just forgot
my car keys.

00:04:54.434 --> 00:04:55.901
-Oh, well, that's enough.

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:58.968
Will someone just tell me who
the new speaker of the House is?

00:04:58.968 --> 00:05:01.501
-My name is Lewis.

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:04.033
[ Laughter ]

00:05:04.033 --> 00:05:08.000
The new speaker is Lewis,
the target Halloween decoration?

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:09.734
I am not the speaker.

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:12.033
My name is Lewis.

00:05:12.033 --> 00:05:13.434
-Okay, good. You know,
I think we're done here.

00:05:13.434 --> 00:05:15.200
Give it up for the new
speaker of the House, Lewis.

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:19.501
[ Applause ]

00:05:19.501 --> 00:05:21.801
Listen to this --
apparently, Netflix plans

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:23.501
to open their own stores

00:05:23.501 --> 00:05:27.267
where customers can play games,
shop, and eat.

00:05:27.267 --> 00:05:30.100
Yeah, they'll even have servers
going up to tables going,

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.300
"Are you still eating?
3, 2, 1..."

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:36.334
[ Laughter ]

00:05:36.334 --> 00:05:37.868
Of course, since it's Netflix,
people are like,

00:05:37.868 --> 00:05:40.200
"We like to skip the appetizers,
go right to the main course."

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:41.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:41.300 --> 00:05:42.868
The only rule at
the Netflix restaurant is,

00:05:42.868 --> 00:05:44.300
you can't share your food.

00:05:44.300 --> 00:05:47.400
[ Laughter, audience groans ]

00:05:47.400 --> 00:05:49.834
Hey, I read that Jeff Bezos
just bought

00:05:49.834 --> 00:05:54.634
his Florida neighbor's mansion
for $79 million.

00:05:54.634 --> 00:05:57.601
Jeff Bezos is the only person
who sees an $80 million mansion

00:05:57.601 --> 00:06:01.200
and goes, "Closet?"
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.200 --> 00:06:03.968
And finally, a man
pleading guilty to stealing

00:06:03.968 --> 00:06:07.501
the "Wizard of Oz" ruby slippers
from a museum in Minnesota.

00:06:07.501 --> 00:06:10.400
Yeah. Or as he tells
his cellmate, "Murder.

00:06:10.400 --> 00:06:13.234
I'm in for murder."
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:06:13.234 --> 00:06:15.467
We have a great show.
Kelly Clarkson

00:06:15.467 --> 00:06:18.133
is here to talk and perform
a song off her new album!

00:06:18.133 --> 00:06:19.400
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:22.767
New York Rangers legend
Henrik Lundqvist is here!

00:06:22.767 --> 00:06:24.234
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:25.501
Let's go write some
thank-you notes.

00:06:25.501 --> 00:06:26.734
Come on, everybody.

00:06:26.734 --> 00:06:29.033
-♪ Riggity rock
is my favorite cartoon ♪

00:06:29.033 --> 00:06:31.133
♪ Aftermath is a honeymoon ♪

00:06:31.133 --> 00:06:32.167
♪ Ay, yo, me, oh, my ♪

00:06:32.167 --> 00:06:33.434
♪ Just gag me with a spoon ♪

00:06:33.434 --> 00:06:36.501
♪♪

00:06:36.501 --> 00:06:38.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:38.767 --> 00:06:41.868
-Hey, everybody, welcome!

00:06:41.868 --> 00:06:44.834
I went to go see
a "Gutenberg!" last night.

00:06:44.834 --> 00:06:46.133
-Ooh! How was it?
-This is --

00:06:46.133 --> 00:06:48.701
This is my actual one.
See, it's all -- it's all --

00:06:48.701 --> 00:06:50.501
I thought I'd get a nice,
new crisp one,

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:51.834
but this is the one I had.

00:06:51.834 --> 00:06:53.734
Was moving around.
I didn't put it in my pocket.

00:06:53.734 --> 00:06:55.033
-It's got
the opening night sticker.

00:06:55.033 --> 00:06:56.634
-When you go to opening night,
you get the sticker.

00:06:56.634 --> 00:06:58.701
So that's what I wanted
to show off. Yeah.

00:06:58.701 --> 00:07:01.801
You got that special sticker.
It was unbelievable.

00:07:01.801 --> 00:07:03.200
They were hilarious.
It was great.

00:07:03.200 --> 00:07:05.634
Was that the James Earl Jones
Theatre here in Broadway?

00:07:05.634 --> 00:07:07.534
I haven't been to a Broadway
play in a little bit,

00:07:07.534 --> 00:07:10.400
so, I mean, the show
has been off for five months,

00:07:10.400 --> 00:07:13.200
so I haven't really been around,
but it was so great.

00:07:13.200 --> 00:07:16.033
I loved everyone
that put on this --

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:18.267
the play and everyone
that works here around.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:21.033
I just miss Broadway.
I love seeing the red carpet.

00:07:21.033 --> 00:07:24.534
I saw the Broadway.com guy.
I love that guy. He's fantastic.

00:07:24.534 --> 00:07:27.300
I saw him.
I was -- It was --

00:07:27.300 --> 00:07:28.734
I saw Anna Wintour.

00:07:28.734 --> 00:07:31.067
-Ooh.
-Sat in front of Anna.

00:07:31.067 --> 00:07:33.334
-Ooh!
-No big deal.

00:07:33.334 --> 00:07:35.300
It's not a big deal, right?
Who cares?

00:07:35.300 --> 00:07:36.634
No one -- No one's asking.

00:07:36.634 --> 00:07:38.601
-Did you --
Who did you sit in front of?

00:07:38.601 --> 00:07:40.467
-Oh, Anna?
-Anna who?

00:07:40.467 --> 00:07:42.067
-Oh, Anna Wintour.
You ever heard of "Vogue"?

00:07:42.067 --> 00:07:43.367
-Oh, my gosh.
-She was behind me

00:07:43.367 --> 00:07:45.167
the whole time.
-Really?

00:07:45.167 --> 00:07:47.801
-No, not a big deal.
So I guess I got good seats.

00:07:47.801 --> 00:07:50.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:50.868 --> 00:07:53.400
It was
the James Earl Jones Theatre.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:55.767
And if you're a fan
of James Earl Jones

00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:58.133
or even "Star Wars"
at the beginning,

00:07:58.133 --> 00:08:00.534
they have a funny joke
that's really good,

00:08:00.534 --> 00:08:02.300
but you just have to
listen to it. It's very --

00:08:02.300 --> 00:08:04.334
But it's all --
There's all jokes spread out.

00:08:04.334 --> 00:08:07.200
It's crazy, by the way.
The play is nuts.

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:09.968
It's absolutely -- it's about
two guys are pitching a play,

00:08:09.968 --> 00:08:12.267
and they know nothing
about Gutenberg

00:08:12.267 --> 00:08:15.868
and the printing press,
and it's -- it's bizarre.

00:08:15.868 --> 00:08:17.200
[ Laughter ]

00:08:17.200 --> 00:08:19.033
But these guys
are so charming and funny.

00:08:19.033 --> 00:08:21.467
Oh, my gosh, everything.
Just a thousand laughs.

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:23.868
So, congratulations to everyone
over at "Gutenberg!"

00:08:23.868 --> 00:08:26.567
and James Earl Jones Theatre.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:26.567 --> 00:08:32.100
And, Anna, call me if you want
to go see a show.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.367
Guys, today's Friday,
that's usually

00:08:33.367 --> 00:08:34.934
when I catch up
on some personal stuff.

00:08:34.934 --> 00:08:37.367
I check my inbox,
I return some e-mails,

00:08:37.367 --> 00:08:39.133
and, of course,
I send out thank-you notes.

00:08:39.133 --> 00:08:42.067
And I was just wondering
if you guys wouldn't mind.

00:08:42.067 --> 00:08:46.033
I like to write out
some thank-you notes right now.

00:08:46.033 --> 00:08:47.400
James, can I have some
thank-you-note

00:08:47.400 --> 00:08:48.400
writing music, please?

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.901
♪♪

00:08:49.901 --> 00:08:51.701
[ Laughter ]

00:08:51.701 --> 00:08:52.801
-Wow.
-Yeah, that's good.

00:08:52.801 --> 00:08:54.334
Could you do it in, like,
an organ style?

00:08:54.334 --> 00:08:57.434
Can you play, like...
♪ Vmm vmm vmm vmm ♪

00:08:57.434 --> 00:09:01.267
♪ Vmm vmm vmm vmm,
Vmm vmm vmm vmm ♪

00:09:01.267 --> 00:09:03.701
♪ Vmm vmm vmm vmm ♪

00:09:03.701 --> 00:09:05.133
♪♪

00:09:05.133 --> 00:09:06.334
Am I not hearing it?

00:09:06.334 --> 00:09:07.367
-I can't hear it.

00:09:07.367 --> 00:09:12.601
♪♪

00:09:12.601 --> 00:09:13.834
[ Musical flourish plays ]

00:09:13.834 --> 00:09:15.701
Oh!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:15.701 --> 00:09:18.000
[ Laughing ]
[ Ding! ]

00:09:18.000 --> 00:09:20.100
Yeah!

00:09:20.100 --> 00:09:21.868
That's the jam right there.

00:09:21.868 --> 00:09:24.167
♪ Ba da boo wop a wow ♪

00:09:24.167 --> 00:09:28.467
♪ Ba da boo bop a bow,
ba da boo bop a bow ♪

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:31.534
♪ Ba da boo bop a bow ♪

00:09:31.534 --> 00:09:36.100
♪ Ba da boo bop a bow,
ba da boo bop a bow ♪

00:09:36.100 --> 00:09:38.634
♪ Ba da boo bop a bow ♪

00:09:38.634 --> 00:09:40.067
There we go.

00:09:40.067 --> 00:09:41.501
Oh, yeah.
-Oh. What's that?

00:09:41.501 --> 00:09:43.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:43.534 --> 00:09:44.834
You sat in front of her?

00:09:44.834 --> 00:09:46.300
-Yeah, she was right there.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:46.300 --> 00:09:48.267
-Wow.
Those are good seats.

00:09:48.267 --> 00:09:49.601
-Moving her head around,
trying to see...

00:09:49.601 --> 00:09:51.133
-'Cause you're wearing
your giant hat that you wear.

00:09:51.133 --> 00:09:52.334
-Yeah, I was
wearing my hairpiece.

00:09:52.334 --> 00:09:55.634
Yeah, exactly.
[ Laughter ]

00:09:55.634 --> 00:09:59.601
No, she's very lovely. I do --
I do love running into her.

00:09:59.601 --> 00:10:01.767
But it was a good crowd.
It was super fun.

00:10:01.767 --> 00:10:04.334
Yeah, it was great.
But, you know, I...

00:10:04.334 --> 00:10:05.734
I just had a better view
than she did.

00:10:05.734 --> 00:10:07.400
-Yeah. Whatever.
Yeah, right.

00:10:07.400 --> 00:10:08.701
Not a big deal.
-We saw the same thing.

00:10:08.701 --> 00:10:09.701
-Yeah, sure.
-Kind of.

00:10:09.701 --> 00:10:10.868
-Yeah.
But you saw better --

00:10:10.868 --> 00:10:13.467
Your view was about
one foot better. Yeah.

00:10:13.467 --> 00:10:14.801
-Less.
-Oh, sure.

00:10:14.801 --> 00:10:15.968
-Less than one foot.
But just --

00:10:15.968 --> 00:10:18.200
Let's just say "better."
-All right.

00:10:18.200 --> 00:10:20.367
Like that, I could --
we could touch hands.

00:10:20.367 --> 00:10:21.667
-Right?
You could reach or you'd reach

00:10:21.667 --> 00:10:23.400
back and touch hands.
-Yeah. I had to reach back

00:10:23.400 --> 00:10:25.834
and strain myself.
[ Laughter ]

00:10:25.834 --> 00:10:28.167
And normally,
if we went together...

00:10:28.167 --> 00:10:29.300
-Right, she'd be sitting
next to you.

00:10:29.300 --> 00:10:30.601
-Yeah.
We could hold hands here.

00:10:30.601 --> 00:10:31.834
-Right.
But no.

00:10:31.834 --> 00:10:33.467
-No.
-Back seat.

00:10:33.467 --> 00:10:34.734
-I shouldn't even be
holding her hand at all.

00:10:34.734 --> 00:10:37.067
It wasn't a scary play.
It was --

00:10:37.067 --> 00:10:38.501
I had no business
holding her hand.

00:10:38.501 --> 00:10:39.934
-But you were anyway?

00:10:39.934 --> 00:10:42.067
-I think it was her hand.
I didn't look behind me.

00:10:42.067 --> 00:10:43.300
-You just put your hand
out like this?

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:45.267
Somebody grabbed it?
-Yeah, someone grabbed it.

00:10:45.267 --> 00:10:46.701
-I was nervous.
-Yeah.

00:10:46.701 --> 00:10:48.000
-I was nervous.
I haven't seen a live play

00:10:48.000 --> 00:10:49.167
in a long time.
-Yeah, you haven't seen one

00:10:49.167 --> 00:10:51.267
in five months.
-I was getting scared.

00:10:51.267 --> 00:10:53.634
I go, "What's all these lights?"
-Especially because today --

00:10:53.634 --> 00:10:55.868
That was Friday the 13th Eve
yesterday.

00:10:55.868 --> 00:10:58.100
-Yeah. By the time -- if I --
if the play went long,

00:10:58.100 --> 00:10:59.300
I would have been there
on Friday the 13th.

00:10:59.300 --> 00:11:00.534
-Yeah.

00:11:00.534 --> 00:11:03.467
-Scary.
-It ended around 8:39.

00:11:03.467 --> 00:11:06.767
-What?
8:39 exactly?

00:11:06.767 --> 00:11:08.067
-Yeah.
-Wow.

00:11:08.067 --> 00:11:10.934
-8:39.
Union rules.

00:11:10.934 --> 00:11:12.968
-Oh, really?
-Every Broadway show has to end

00:11:12.968 --> 00:11:14.634
at 8:39.
-8:39, wow.

00:11:14.634 --> 00:11:17.167
-Yeah.
On Thursday the 12th.

00:11:17.167 --> 00:11:18.434
-Thursday the 12th. Yeah.

00:11:18.434 --> 00:11:21.534
-It was good.
You should go see it.

00:11:21.534 --> 00:11:22.534
-I will.

00:11:22.534 --> 00:11:23.767
♪♪

00:11:23.767 --> 00:11:27.467
[ Laughter ]

00:11:27.467 --> 00:11:28.834
-Save it, save it.

00:11:28.834 --> 00:11:31.834
[ Applause ]

00:11:31.834 --> 00:11:33.400
Ready?

00:11:33.400 --> 00:11:35.534
[ Clears throat ]
-[ Clears throat ]

00:11:35.534 --> 00:11:37.634
♪♪

00:11:37.634 --> 00:11:39.734
-Thank you, autumn,

00:11:39.734 --> 00:11:41.767
for being fall's legal name.

00:11:41.767 --> 00:11:44.267
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:44.267 --> 00:11:48.400
-Like a nickname.
-Autumn Jo Smith.

00:11:48.400 --> 00:11:49.634
♪♪

00:11:49.634 --> 00:11:52.834
-Thank you, scarves,
for being the only clothes

00:11:52.834 --> 00:11:54.834
that you put on with attitude.

00:11:54.834 --> 00:11:58.067
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:11:58.067 --> 00:12:01.033
-Really?
Why not?

00:12:01.033 --> 00:12:03.100
-Why not?

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:04.367
♪♪

00:12:04.367 --> 00:12:08.000
-Thank you, step ladders.
You're not my real ladder,

00:12:08.000 --> 00:12:10.634
but I can tell you
make my mom very happy.

00:12:10.634 --> 00:12:13.534
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:12:13.534 --> 00:12:16.100
♪♪

00:12:16.100 --> 00:12:19.701
-"Get away from me!
You're not my real ladder!"

00:12:19.701 --> 00:12:23.734
[ Laughter ]

00:12:23.734 --> 00:12:25.167
-"This is my step ladder, Doug."

00:12:25.167 --> 00:12:28.400
[ Laughter ]

00:12:28.400 --> 00:12:29.734
♪♪

00:12:29.734 --> 00:12:32.767
Thank you, British TV shows,
for reminding me

00:12:32.767 --> 00:12:34.100
that just because
it's in English

00:12:34.100 --> 00:12:36.167
doesn't mean
I don't need subtitles.

00:12:36.167 --> 00:12:40.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:12:40.767 --> 00:12:45.067
[ Gibberish ]

00:12:45.067 --> 00:12:46.133
-Huh?

00:12:46.133 --> 00:12:49.267
[ Laughter ]

00:12:49.267 --> 00:12:50.501
♪♪

00:12:50.501 --> 00:12:53.634
Thank you,
being offered banana bread,

00:12:53.634 --> 00:12:55.801
for being told all
of our bananas started to rot,

00:12:55.801 --> 00:12:59.334
so, well, here you go.
Enjoy that."

00:12:59.334 --> 00:13:01.534
-Live it up.
-You don't have to tell me that.

00:13:01.534 --> 00:13:02.801
-Yeah.
-"Yeah, they're all going bad,

00:13:02.801 --> 00:13:05.033
so we made this for you."
[ Laughter ]

00:13:05.033 --> 00:13:07.367
-They were moldy.
-[ Chuckles ]

00:13:07.367 --> 00:13:10.901
Thank you, V.R. headsets
for being the coolest way

00:13:10.901 --> 00:13:12.968
to look like you're wearing
a jockstrap on your head.

00:13:12.968 --> 00:13:16.167
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:16.167 --> 00:13:19.868
-Hey! Oh!

00:13:19.868 --> 00:13:21.334
It smells ripe.

00:13:21.334 --> 00:13:23.734
[ Laughter ]

00:13:23.734 --> 00:13:24.868
♪♪

00:13:24.868 --> 00:13:27.901
-Thank you,
plastic vampire teeth,

00:13:27.901 --> 00:13:30.133
for being Dracula's Invisalign.

00:13:30.133 --> 00:13:33.801
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:33.801 --> 00:13:35.434
Couldn't have done that joke
10 years ago.

00:13:35.434 --> 00:13:38.000
-Yeah.

00:13:38.000 --> 00:13:39.200
♪♪

00:13:39.200 --> 00:13:41.567
-Thank you,
kids who carve pumpkins

00:13:41.567 --> 00:13:43.567
with super elaborate designs,

00:13:43.567 --> 00:13:45.434
for making me think,
"That's really impressive,"

00:13:45.434 --> 00:13:47.968
as well as,
"Do not anger this kid."

00:13:47.968 --> 00:13:53.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:13:53.400 --> 00:13:55.567
-[ Laughs ]
Oh!

00:13:55.567 --> 00:13:57.133
[ Laughter ]

00:13:57.133 --> 00:13:59.267
-[ Chuckles ]
Thank you,

00:13:59.267 --> 00:14:01.901
the moment I finally
get comfortable in bed,

00:14:01.901 --> 00:14:03.734
for also being the moment
my bladder goes,

00:14:03.734 --> 00:14:06.100
"Guess what."
There you have it, everybody.

00:14:06.100 --> 00:14:07.467
Those are my thank-you notes.

